# Starwind Triggers — Button Styling

When a Starwind trigger (`SheetTrigger`, `DialogTrigger`, `PopoverTrigger`, etc.) should look like a button, **do not** use `asChild` with a nested `<Button>`. Style the trigger itself with `ButtonVariants.button`.

```astro
import {ButtonVariants} from "@/components/starwind/button";

<!-- ❌ BAD — asChild + separate Button -->
<SheetTrigger asChild>
	<Button variant="outline" size="icon-sm" aria-label="Menu">
		<Menu />
	</Button>
</SheetTrigger>

<!-- ✅ GOOD — ButtonVariants on the trigger -->
<SheetTrigger class={ButtonVariants.button({ variant: "outline", size: "icon-sm" })} aria-label="Menu">
	<Menu />
</SheetTrigger>
```

- Import: `import { ButtonVariants } from "@/components/starwind/button";`
- Pass `variant` / `size` (and extra classes via `tv` `class` if needed) into `ButtonVariants.button({ … })`.
- Keep using `<Button>` for real buttons/links that are not Starwind triggers.
